  "query_preview": ".. /Monday through Friday/... The low pressure system \nnear Haida Gwaii is expected to meander westward before another \nlow forms near Prince William Sound. The secondary low near \nAnchorage is expected to move southward, and push the initial low \ncloser to the Alaska Panhandle next week. This means that a fairly\nwet weather pattern is expected through next week. \n\nHowever, the exact placement of these low pressure systems will \ndictate who has the highest chances for rain and strongest winds \nacross Southeast Alaska. As of now, the Southern Panhandle looks to \nhave the highest rain chances, and perhaps some stronger winds (up \nto 20 kts) in Clarence Strait. Overall, the rainfall totals don't \nlook particularly impactful, but it will be monitored for future \nforecast updates.",
